          "authorityIds": "col:55LLB,wfo:wfo-0000321537",
          "description": "A creeping perennial herb (family Tetrachondraceae, order Lamiales) endemic to New Zealand, rooting at the nodes to form turf-like patches; stems are fleshy and square in cross-section, leaves opposite and fleshy (~2 x 2 mm), with solitary off-white to greenish-white flowers and fruit of four brown setulose nutlets. It grows in open damp turf along lake and tarn margins, flushes and seepages in the North and South Islands and Stewart Island. NZTCS: Threatened - Nationally Vulnerable."
        },
