          "authorityIds": "col:55LLC,wfo:wfo-0000321538",
          "description": "An accepted species of Tetrachondraceae (order Lamiales), described by Carl Skottsberg in 1912 from southern South America. It is the South American vicariant of the otherwise New Zealand genus Tetrachondra, a small, low creeping or mat-forming perennial herb native to Patagonia and Tierra del Fuego."
